.SH NAME
PerformanceContainerTiming.presentationTime \-
PerformanceContainerTiming: presentationTime property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]presentationTime\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]PerformanceContainerTiming\f[R] interface returns the
\f[CR]timestamp\f[R] when the container\(cqs newly painted content was
actually drawn on the screen.
.PP
The \f[CR]presentationTime\f[R] value is nullable: the underlying
timestamp is implementation\-defined, so browsers that don\(cqt populate
it return \f[CR]null\f[R] instead.
Because \f[CR]PerformanceContainerTiming.paintTime\f[R] is always
populated the same way across implementations, it\(cqs the more reliable
value to use for metrics that need to be comparable across browsers.
.SH VALUE
A \f[CR]DOMHighResTimeStamp\f[R], or \f[CR]null\f[R] if the value is not
exposed.
.SH EXAMPLES
See Observing how entries change as a container grows.
